course: dictionary
lesson: 106
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Adjourn is a formal word. Its main meaning is to stop something for a while and carry on later. «The court adjourned until the next day» means the judge stopped the case and it started again the next day.
explain: The clues are in the words around it: a court, a meeting, a game, until the next day. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning, "stop for now", in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The second meaning is jokey: to adjourn to a place is to move there together. «Let's adjourn to the kitchen» means let's all go to the kitchen. In «I move that the meeting adjourn», the Dodo means: let's stop this meeting and try something more lively straight away.
fact: Adjourn means to stop for a while and continue later.
fact: «The court adjourned until the next day.»
fact: In everyday talk you might say "break", "stop for now" or "put off" instead.
fact: «Let's adjourn to the kitchen» is a jokey way of saying let's all go to the kitchen together.
fact: Forms of the verb: adjourn, adjourns, adjourned, adjourning.
exercise: «The court adjourned until the next day.» What does adjourned mean here? | *Stopped for now and carried on later | Got married | Lost the case forever | Ran quickly out of the room
exercise: Jessa's teacher says, «Let's adjourn to the library.» What does adjourn mean in this sentence? | To stop reading for ever | To borrow books and sit in silence | To close the library door | *To move there together
exercise: Which everyday words could replace adjourn in «the meeting adjourned at four o'clock»? | ran | shouted | *stopped for now | grew
test: The school council will adjourn its meeting to next week. What does adjourn mean? | *Stop the meeting and carry on next week | Move the meeting into a bigger hall | Start the meeting early | Cancel the council forever
test: Which everyday phrase is closest in meaning to adjourn? | *Stop for now | Fall asleep | Ask a question | Begin loudly
exam: The judge adjourned the case. Which word best replaces adjourned? | Ended for ever | Forgot | Shouted | *Paused until later
